      "Explanation": "The correct answer is C (2, 3, 1). Explanation: - Stage 2 (High birth rate with a high death rate): This is the first stage (Pre-industrial) of the demographic transition. In this stage, both birth and death rates are high, resulting in a stable or slow-growing population. This is common in agrarian societies with limited medical care and technology. - Stage 3 (High birth rate with a low death rate): This corresponds to the second stage (Transitional) of the model. As a country begins to develop, improvements in healthcare, sanitation, and food supply lead to a sharp decline in death rates, while birth rates remain high, causing a population explosion. - Stage 1 (Low birth rate with a low death rate): This represents the final stages (Industrial or Post-industrial) of the transition. As society becomes more urbanized and technologically advanced, birth rates decline to match the low death rates, leading to a stable and older population.",
