      "Explanation": "The correct answer is D (1, 2 and 3). Explanation: - Statement 1 is correct: As the banker to banks, the RBI maintains the cash reserves of commercial banks. All scheduled commercial banks are required to keep a certain percentage of their deposits (Cash Reserve Ratio or CRR) with the RBI. - Statement 2 is correct: The RBI acts as the \"Lender of the Last Resort.\" When commercial banks face a liquidity crunch or financial stress and cannot obtain funds from other sources, they can borrow from the RBI against approved securities. - Statement 3 is correct: The RBI performs an advisory role for commercial banks. It provides guidance and directions on monetary matters, credit control, and various banking policies to ensure the stability of the financial system.",
