      "Explanation": "The correct answer is C (2, 3 and 4 only). Explanation: - Statement 1 is incorrect: Permitting Non-Banking Financial Companies (NBFCs) to do banking is primarily a regulatory and financial sector reform. While it may indirectly support financial inclusion, it is not considered an essential part of the structural framework of inclusive governance. - Statement 2 is correct: Establishing effective District Planning Committees (DPCs) is a key part of inclusive governance. DPCs facilitate decentralized planning and ensure that local needs from both rural (Panchayats) and urban (Municipalities) areas are integrated into the development process, promoting participatory decision-making. - Statement 3 is correct: Increasing government spending on public health is essential for inclusive governance as it ensures that basic services are accessible to all sections of society, particularly the marginalized and vulnerable who rely on public systems for their well-being. - Statement 4 is correct: Strengthening the Mid-day Meal Scheme is a part of inclusive governance because it targets social equity. By providing nutritional support to children from disadvantaged backgrounds, it improves health and educational outcomes, ensuring that the benefits of growth are shared broadly.",
