      "Option D": "an increase in the level of income and employment",
      "Answer": "B",
      "Explanation": "The correct answer is B (an increase in the rate of interest). Explanation: - The money market equilibrium is determined by the intersection of the money supply and money demand curves. - In this scenario, the money supply is fixed (represented by a vertical curve) because it is controlled by the central bank and does not change regardless of interest rates. - An increase in the demand for money (a rightward shift of the downward-sloping demand curve) means that at the original interest rate, people want to hold more money than is currently available. - To obtain more cash, individuals and businesses sell other financial assets, such as bonds. As the supply of bonds increases, bond prices fall. - Because bond prices and interest rates are inversely related, the fall in bond prices causes the nominal interest rate to rise. - The interest rate will continue to increase until the quantity of money demanded decreases to match the fixed money supply, establishing a new equilibrium at a higher interest rate.",
