      "Explanation": "The correct answer is D (Renminbi). Explanation: - The Special Drawing Right (SDR) is an international reserve asset created by the IMF. Its value is based on a basket of five key currencies. - Historically, the basket consisted of the U.S. dollar, the euro, the Japanese yen, and the British pound sterling. - In 2015, the IMF Executive Board concluded a five-year review and decided to include the Chinese Renminbi (yuan) in the SDR basket. - The Renminbi officially joined the basket on October 1, 2016, becoming the fifth currency in the valuation stable alongside the existing four major international currencies.",
