      "Answer": "A",
      "Explanation": "The correct answer is A. WTO affairs. Explanation: - The terms ‘amber box, blue box and green box’ refer to categories of domestic subsidies for agriculture under the World Trade Organization (WTO) Agreement on Agriculture. - Amber Box: Includes all domestic support measures that are considered to distort production and trade. These include price support and subsidies directly related to production quantities. WTO members are required to reduce these supports. - Blue Box: This is considered the ‘amber box with conditions.’ It includes subsidies that would normally be in the amber box but are placed here because they require farmers to limit production. There are currently no spending limits on these subsidies. - Green Box: Includes subsidies that cause no or minimal trade distortion. These must be government-funded and cannot involve price support. Examples include research funding, environmental protection, and direct income support for farmers that is not linked to current production levels. These subsidies are allowed without limits.",
