      "Explanation": "The correct answer is D. To aim at faster resolution of stressed assets of Rs. 50 crore or more which are under consortium lending Explanation: - The Inter-Creditor Agreement (ICA) was signed by Indian banks and financial institutions as part of \"Project Sashakt,\" a plan approved by the government to address the problem of resolving non-performing assets (bad loans). - The agreement was based on the recommendations of the Sunil Mehta Committee, which identified disagreement among multiple lenders as a major hurdle in resolving debt. - The ICA specifically targets loan accounts with a size of Rs. 50 crore or more that are under the control of a group of lenders (consortium lending). - Under the agreement, if 66% of the lenders (by value) agree to a resolution plan, it becomes binding on all lenders, thereby preventing individual creditors from stalling the recovery or restructuring process.",
