      "Explanation": "The correct answer is D. A foreign company transfers shares and such shares derive their substantial value from assets located in India Explanation: - Indirect transfer refers to the sale of shares or interest in a foreign entity (incorporated outside India) that derives its value substantially from assets located in India. - Under Section 9(1)(i) of the Income-tax Act, 1961, income from such transfers is deemed to accrue or arise in India and is therefore subject to Indian capital gains tax. - For the provision to apply, the \"substantial value\" test must be met: the fair market value of Indian assets must exceed Rs 10 crore and represent at least 50% of the value of all assets owned by the foreign company. - This legal framework was notably introduced and clarified in the wake of high-profile tax disputes like the Vodafone case to ensure that the source jurisdiction (India) can tax gains from the transfer of underlying Indian assets, even when the transaction occurs offshore between non-residents.",
