      "Answer": "B",
      "Explanation": "The correct answer is B. Explanation: - The concept of Small Farmer Large Field (SFLF) is a collective action model designed to help small and marginal farmers overcome disadvantages related to diseconomies of scale and lack of bargaining power. - Under this model, farmers in a specific area organize themselves into informal groups to synchronize and harmonize agricultural operations such as nursery bed management, transplanting, and harvesting. - By coordinating these activities and pooling their small landholdings into a single large patch or \"field,\" farmers can utilize mechanization more effectively and achieve economies of scale similar to large-scale farming. - This collective approach also empowers farmers to purchase inputs like seeds and fertilizers in bulk and sell their produce as a group, significantly increasing their bargaining power in price negotiations.",
