      "Explanation": "The correct answer is C (Fair application of law). Explanation: - Option C is correct: In essence, \"due process of law\" refers to the fair application of the law. It is a fundamental principle ensuring that all legal proceedings will be fair and that individuals will be given notice of the proceedings and an opportunity to be heard before the government acts to take away their life, liberty, or property. It acts as a safeguard from arbitrary denial of rights by the government. - Option A is incorrect: While the concept of natural justice is similar and related, particularly in other jurisdictions, \"due process of law\" is the specific legal doctrine used in the United States and historically derived from English law to ensure fairness in legal procedures. - Option B is incorrect: \"Procedure established by law\" is a narrower term that implies following the specific steps laid out in a statute. \"Due process of law\" is broader, encompassing both procedural fairness and substantive rights, ensuring the law itself is fair and just. - Option D is incorrect: \"Equality before law\" means that all people are subject to the same laws in the same manner. While due process helps ensure this, it specifically focuses on the fairness of the legal process and the protection against arbitrary government action.",
