      "Explanation": "The correct answer is C (The e-Waste Management and Handling Rules, 2011). Explanation: - Extended Producer Responsibility (EPR) was formally introduced in India as a significant feature under the e-Waste (Management and Handling) Rules, 2011. - This policy framework makes producers responsible for the entire lifecycle of their products, particularly for the collection, recycling, and environmentally sound disposal of electronic waste at the end of its life. - While concepts like the \"polluter pays\" principle existed earlier, the 2011 e-Waste rules were the first to codify EPR as a mandatory regulatory requirement for manufacturers and importers in a specific sector. - Since its introduction in 2011, the EPR framework has been expanded to cover other waste streams in India, including plastic packaging (under the 2016 rules), batteries, and tires.",
