      "Explanation": "The correct answer is D. Waste-to-energy technologies. Explanation: - Pyrolysis is a thermochemical process that involves the thermal decomposition of organic matter in the absence of oxygen. It converts waste materials into solid char, liquid bio-oil, and combustible syngas. - Plasma gasification is a waste treatment technology that uses extremely high temperatures, generated by plasma torches or arcs, to break down waste into its elemental components. This process transforms organic matter into syngas (primarily hydrogen and carbon monoxide) and inorganic matter into a vitrified slag. - Both terms are frequently mentioned in the context of waste management and waste-to-energy technologies because they provide alternatives to traditional incineration for recovering energy and resources from various waste streams, including municipal solid waste, hazardous waste, and biomass.",
