      "Explanation": "The correct answer is C (Honeybees). Explanation: - Honeybees use a sophisticated form of communication known as the waggle dance to share information with their nestmates about the location of resources like nectar, pollen, or water. - The dance follows a figure-eight pattern. The central part of the dance, called the waggle run, is where the bee vigorously shakes its abdomen while moving forward. - The angle of the waggle run relative to the vertical hive indicates the direction of the food source in relation to the sun's position. - The duration of the waggle run communicates the distance to the food source; generally, a longer run indicates a greater distance. - This behavior is a form of social learning, as younger bees must observe experienced foragers to refine their dancing accuracy and correctly encode distance and direction.",
