      "Explanation": "All three organisms—Cicada, Froghopper, and Pond skater—are classified as insects. They belong to the class Insecta and the order Hemiptera, commonly known as true bugs. - Cicada: Large, winged insects known for the loud acoustic signals produced by males using drum-like organs called tymbals. - Froghopper: Also known as spittlebugs, these are jumping insects famous for their nymphs, which produce a protective foam or \"spittle.\" - Pond Skater: Also known as water striders, these aquatic insects use surface tension and hydrophobic hairs on their legs to walk or \"skate\" on the surface of water.",
