      "Set Question": "",
      "Subject": "Science & Technology",
      "Unit": "Biotechnology",
      "Topic": "Genetic Engineering",
      "Topic ID": "SNT-U01-T01",
      "Question": "A genetically engineered form of brinjal, known as the Bt-brinjal, has been developed. The objective of this is -",
      "Option A": "To make it pest-resistant",
      "Option B": "To improve its taste and nutritive qualities",
      "Option C": "To make it drought-resistant",
      "Option D": "To make its shelf-life longer",
      "Answer": "A",
      "Explanation": "The correct answer is A. To make it pest-resistant. Explanation: - Genetic Engineering: Bt-brinjal is a transgenic crop created by inserting the cry1Ac gene from the soil bacterium Bacillus thuringiensis (Bt) into the brinjal plant's genome. - Pest Resistance: The primary objective of this modification is to provide resistance against lepidopteran insects, specifically the Brinjal Fruit and Shoot Borer (FSB), which is a major pest that significantly reduces crop yields. - Mechanism of Action: When the larvae of these pests ingest the Bt protein produced by the plant, the protein is activated in their alkaline gut, leading to the breakdown of the gut wall and the eventual death of the insect. - Benefits: By being naturally pest-resistant, Bt-brinjal reduces the need for frequent chemical insecticide applications, leading to higher marketable yields and lower production costs for farmers.",
      "Difficulty": "Unlabelled"
