      "Explanation": "The correct answer is C (1 and 3 only). Explanation: - Statement 1 is correct: CFLs (Compact Fluorescent Lamps) produce light by driving an electric current through a tube containing mercury vapor and argon, which creates UV light that excites a phosphor coating to emit visible light. In contrast, LEDs (Light Emitting Diodes) produce light by passing an electric current through a semiconductor material. - Statement 2 is incorrect: The average lifespan of an LED lamp is significantly longer than that of a CFL. LEDs typically last between 25,000 to 50,000 hours, whereas CFLs generally last around 8,000 to 10,000 hours. - Statement 3 is correct: CFLs are less energy-efficient than LED lamps because they release a large portion (approximately 80%) of their energy as heat, while LEDs emit very little heat and convert more energy directly into light.",
