      "Option B": "2 only",
      "Option C": "1, 2 and 3",
      "Option D": "None of the above statements is correct",
      "Answer": "C",
      "Explanation": "The correct answer is C (1, 2 and 3). Explanation: - Statement 1 is correct: OLED displays use organic compounds that emit light when an electric current is applied. Because these organic layers are thinner and lighter than the crystalline layers used in LCDs, they can be fabricated on flexible plastic substrates (like polyimide) instead of rigid glass. - Statement 2 is correct: The use of flexible plastic substrates allows OLED displays to be bent, folded, or rolled. This flexibility enables the creation of roll-up displays that can be integrated into curved surfaces or even clothing. - Statement 3 is correct: Transparent OLEDs (TOLEDs) use transparent electrodes and a clear substrate. Since OLED pixels are self-emissive and do not require a backlight, the area around the pixels can remain clear, making truly see-through displays possible.",
