      "Option B": "2 and 3 only",
      "Option C": "3 only",
      "Option D": "1, 2 and 3",
      "Answer": "C",
      "Explanation": "The correct answer is B (2 and 3 only). Explanation: - Statement 1 is incorrect: A digital signature is a mathematical algorithm or cryptographic method, not an electronic record that identifies a certifying authority. An electronic record that identifies a certifying authority and binds a public key to an identity is known as a digital certificate. - Statement 2 is correct: Digital signatures are used to identify users and organizations in digital messages or documents. They serve as a secure method to verify the identity of an individual or entity accessing information or servers over the internet, often as part of a broader Public Key Infrastructure (PKI). - Statement 3 is correct: A digital signature is an electronic method of signing a document using a private key. It ensures data integrity because any change to the original content will result in a different hash value, causing the verification process to fail and alerting the recipient that the document has been altered.",
