      "Explanation": "The correct answer is C (Both 1 and 2). Explanation: - Statement 1 is correct: Genetic engineering is a fundamental part of developing recombinant vector vaccines. These vaccines are created by inserting genetic material (DNA) from a pathogen into the genome of a harmless carrier or \"vector.\" This process of altering an organism's genetic code to express foreign antigens is a core application of genetic engineering. - Statement 2 is correct: Both bacteria and viruses are used as vectors in these vaccines. Common viral vectors include adenoviruses (like those used in some COVID-19 vaccines), measles virus, and vaccinia virus. Bacteria, such as Bacille Calmette-Guérin (BCG) or attenuated Salmonella, can also be engineered to act as vectors to deliver antigens into the body.",
