      "Explanation": "The correct answer is D (Neither 1 nor 2). Explanation: - Statement 1 is incorrect: Cruise missiles are jet-propelled (often using ramjet engines) and can fly at subsonic, supersonic, or hypersonic speeds throughout their flight. Ballistic missiles are rocket-powered only during the initial phase of flight, after which they follow an unpowered, arcing trajectory (ballistic path) to their target. The statement incorrectly swaps the propulsion characteristics of the two missile types. - Statement 2 is incorrect: Agni-V is a solid-fuelled intercontinental ballistic missile (ICBM) with a range exceeding 5,000 km. BrahMos is a supersonic cruise missile (not a ballistic missile) with a much shorter range, typically between 290 km and 800 km depending on the variant. The statement incorrectly identifies the types and range categories for both missiles.",
