      "Explanation": "The correct answer is B (3 only). Explanation: - Statement 1 is incorrect: Soil organic matter acts like a sponge and can absorb and hold up to 90 percent of its weight in water. Therefore, high organic matter content increases a soil's water holding capacity rather than reducing it. - Statement 2 is incorrect: Soil plays a vital role in the sulphur cycle. Most soil sulphur (over 95%) is stored in organic matter. Soil microorganisms drive the cycle by transforming these organic forms into inorganic sulphate through mineralization, which is the form plants can absorb. - Statement 3 is correct: Irrigation water contains dissolved salts. When plants use the water or it evaporates, these salts are left behind. Over time, without adequate drainage or leaching, these salts accumulate and lead to the salinization of agricultural lands.",
