      "Explanation": "The correct answer is C. Statement-I is correct but Statement-II is incorrect. Explanation: - Statement-I is correct: According to the United Nations World Water Development Report 2022, India is the world's largest user of groundwater, extracting an estimated 251 cubic kilometers annually. This amount accounts for more than a quarter (approximately 25-26%) of the total global groundwater withdrawal. - Statement-II is incorrect: While India is home to approximately 17-18% of the world's population, its massive groundwater extraction is primarily driven by agriculture rather than drinking water and sanitation needs. Approximately 89% of the groundwater extracted in India is used for irrigation, while only about 11% is used for domestic and industrial purposes combined. Therefore, the need to satisfy drinking water and sanitation requirements is not the primary reason India extracts more than a quarter of the world's groundwater.",
