      "Explanation": "The correct answer is D (1, 2 and 3). Explanation: - Statement 1 is correct: Dispersion is the process where white sunlight is split into its component colors (the visible spectrum) as it enters and travels through the water droplet. - Statement 2 is correct: Refraction occurs when sunlight enters the water droplet and again when it exits, causing the light to bend as it changes speed between the air and the denser water. - Statement 3 is correct: Internal reflection happens when the light hits the back surface of the water droplet and bounces back toward the front of the drop rather than passing straight through. Some sources specify this is partial internal reflection rather than \"total\" internal reflection, but it is the physical phenomenon responsible for directing the light back toward the observer to form the rainbow.",
