      "Option C": "Nitrogen dioxide",
      "Option D": "Nitrogen pentoxide",
      "Answer": "A",
      "Explanation": "Nitric oxide is a gaseous signaling molecule synthesized by endothelial cells lining the blood vessels. It acts as a potent vasodilator by relaxing the inner walls of the blood vessels, particularly the smooth muscle cells. This relaxation causes the vessels to widen, which reduces blood pressure and increases blood flow, ensuring that oxygen and nutrients are efficiently delivered to various organs and tissues. While other nitrogen compounds like nitrous oxide (laughing gas) or nitrogen dioxide exist, nitric oxide is the specific molecule produced by the body to regulate vascular tone and blood flow.",
